From c39b002ad3e7961dce35c2467e507acfde312013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gianni Spadoni <me@gio.blue>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 11:06:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(Hardware Support): Qualcomm SSC sensors through FastRPC

This implements support for the Qualcomm Sensor Core (SSC), which provides
accel and gyro to some Snapdragon based handhelds made in the past 8 years
or so.

This requires libssc as a runtime dependency, and requires libloading as a
build time & runtime dependency.

As FastRPC devices don't actually show up in a "fastrpc" subsystem, and
instead use the "misc" subsystem, some logic has been added to
udev/device.rs to check for fastrpc devices and fake the subsystem.

On top of that: the manager only takes FastRPC devices when
INPUTPLUMBER_FASTRPC=1. Gyro is
passed through in rad/s for the targets to scale. The GLib main context is
drained on every poll, opening keeps retrying until the SSC answers, and
libssc is loaded by its versioned soname. The sensors open at
config.imu.sample_rate, 200 Hz by default; libssc otherwise picks the
first advertised rate, 12.5 Hz or lower on some IMUs. Like the IIO IMU
driver, the driver filters on its own events, maps them through
EventCapability and honours accel_correction and gyro_correction.

Co-authored-by: Radical <radical@radical.fun>
Co-authored-by: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
